// SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
//! The deterministic replay ENGINE.
//!
//! [`crate::replay_cmd`] owns the entry gates + the stable exit-code contract;
//! this module owns everything after the gates pass: runtime construction,
//! external-topic injection, graph-produced-topic capture, the recorded-clock
//! re-advance, the bit-exact diff, and the [`ReplayOutcome`] + report.
//!
//! # The self-contained model
//!
//! The bag is its own golden. Node cdylibs load from the CURRENT workspace
//! build (the workspace build IS the candidate), so replay runs from the
//! workspace root exactly like `cerulion graph run` — a code change that
//! alters a node's output is caught as a byte divergence against the recording.
//!
//! # The recorded-clock re-advance (the headline seam)
//!
//! The recorded scheduler trace carries one STEP_BOUNDARY record per step
//! (`RECORD_TYPE_STEP_BOUNDARY`, kind 3): its `fire_time_ns` is the step's
//! ADVANCED gating-clock value — the `current_time_ns` every same-step publish
//! stamps into its wire `timestamp_ns`. Replay iterates the boundaries in step
//! order and drives [`cerulion_core::GraphRuntime::step`] with the exact
//! per-step delta between consecutive boundary values — so the replayed gating
//! clock retraces the recorded trajectory and the replayed frames come out
//! BYTE-IDENTICAL to the recording (Principle #7: Replay = Live).
//!
//! FIRE records are NOT the clock source: a `Period` fire's `fire_time_ns` is
//! the period BOUNDARY, which under wall-advance recording (the gating clock
//! advanced by MEASURED wall time per live step) is strictly BELOW
//! the step's advanced clock, so `max(fire_time_ns)` per step UNDERSHOOTS the
//! true clock and would stamp different wire timestamps than the recording (a
//! false byte divergence on every frame). Before the replay loop, the recording
//! is cross-checked for internal consistency (`validate_recording_consistency`)
//! — frames vs the boundary set, fires vs their step's boundary, boundary
//! monotonicity — so a corrupt/hand-edited bag fails loudly (exit 2) instead of
//! replaying garbage. The wall clock is never read on the replay loop — every
//! delta comes from the recorded boundaries.
//!
//! # Topic classes
//!
//! Every recorded topic (bag channel, excluding `__cerulion/*`) is classified
//! from the graph:
//! - GRAPH-PRODUCED (an in-graph node output) — re-executed, captured, diffed.
//! - EXTERNAL (consumed in-graph, no in-graph producer: the
//!   absolute `source:` class) — the recorded frames are re-INJECTED byte-exact
//!   so the downstream graph sees the same inputs it saw live.
//! - UNMODELLED (neither, but the bag's own coverage manifest marks it
//!   [`TapSource::Discovered`]) — a live producer the recorder found by service
//!   enumeration and deliberately recorded, which the graph does not model.
//!   SKIPPED (not injected, not diffed) with a loud one-time `warn!`.
//! - Neither, and not marked discovered — the bag and its embedded graph
//!   disagree (corrupt / hand-edited) → [`ReplayError::BagGraphMismatch`]
//!   (exit 2).

